 "about_text": "Sage Culture is an art gallery and multidisciplinary project space in the Arts District of Los Angeles, founded in 2017 by Nicolas Alonso and Marina Figueiredo. The gallery's concept grew out of a trip to Easter Island and centers on the relationship between people and nature, drawing on ancient and primitive forms of artistic expression. Its program represents artists whose work is deeply tied to natural materials, processes, and themes, spanning ceramics, textiles, photography, and mixed media. Works often blur boundaries between art, craft, and design, emphasizing process, material experimentation, and a meditative or ecological sensibility. The gallery operates by appointment only from its DTLA location.",
